bound-lock/1 about="Everything a system says about itself lives where nobody can check it: a config, a README, a CI log. topos is one line format for all of it — a signed line with a floor and a ceiling, that any head can fold and any second head can verify. Two implementations agree only on what passes between them, and what passes between them is a line. So the line is the one thing held still; everything else belongs to a world." at=policy:prose by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/idea value=lock
